{
  // **TSD §2.2 specifies this file, and it now says what the document says.** It had drifted in
  // three ways, only one of which was recorded: it extended `../../tsconfig.base.json` alone,
  // dropped the `@/*` alias, and narrowed `lib` to `["ES2023","DOM"]`. Dropping
  // `expo/tsconfig.base` cost `customConditions: ["react-native"]`, `moduleDetection: "force"`
  // and `allowJs` — no dependency in the tree resolves through a `react-native` exports condition
  // today, so nothing miscompiled, but a document that specifies a file's contents outranks the
  // file (Plan §4: PRD > SDD > TSD > Plan), and `Plan.md` T-01-08's note could not authorise the
  // deviation because the Plan is the lowest rank of the four.
  "extends": ["expo/tsconfig.base", "../../tsconfig.base.json"],
  "compilerOptions": {
    // §2.2: "the only path alias in the repo". A TypeScript alias only — Metro does not resolve
    // it, so runtime imports inside `apps/mobile` stay relative and every one ends in `.js`.
    // It currently has no users; restored because the document names it, not because code needs it.
    "paths": { "@/*": ["./src/*"] },

    // A recorded ADDITION rather than a contradiction — §2.2 fixes `extends` and `paths` and says
    // nothing about `types`. It is required: without it, TypeScript's automatic type inclusion
    // does not reach the root's `@types/node` from this directory, and `node:fs` is not resolved
    // like a module ("skipping module 'node:fs' that looks like an absolute URI") — it exists only
    // as an ambient declaration inside `@types/node`. Its absence broke the four tests that read
    // SOURCE FILES from disk to assert an import boundary or a token/loader agreement:
    // `boundary.test.ts`, `typography.test.ts`, `linking.dom.test.ts`, `asyncStorageDriver.test.ts`.
    //
    // Naming the two global packages is also stricter than discovery: everything else — `vitest`,
    // `@testing-library/dom`, `@types/react-dom` — arrives through ordinary import resolution,
    // which `types` does not affect.
    "types": ["node", "react"]
  },
  // `index.ts` and `App.tsx` sit OUTSIDE `src/`, which is why there is no `rootDir`: it made this
  // project fail outright (`TS6059`) and, with `noEmit`, constrained nothing worth constraining —
  // and while it did, `App.tsx`, `index.ts` and `packages/catalog/seed.ts` were invisible to the
  // gate. `baseUrl` is gone for a different reason: TypeScript 6.0 deprecates it (`TS5101`), and
  // `paths` resolves relative to this file without it.
  // `App.dom.test.tsx` is named for the same reason `App.tsx` is: it sits outside `src/`, so
  // without it a type error in the composition root's only test would never reach
  // `tsc --noEmit -p apps/mobile`. The test was written at P22 and typechecked clean only
  // through a generated throwaway project until this line existed.
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts", "src/**/*.tsx", "index.ts", "App.tsx", "App.dom.test.tsx"]
}
